A oneOf with a null schema among its members: the member is skipped, and every
member after it is still a variant, with its type and its constructor. Found by
the mutation run of 0011-PLAN-engine-tests.md, step 9. The meta declares
$/cancel_request and the schema its smallest definition, which the runtime
needs.

-- meta.json --
{"version": 1, "agentMethods": {}, "clientMethods": {}, "protocolMethods": {"cancel_request": "$/cancel_request"}}
-- schema.json --
{"$defs": {
  "Pair": {"oneOf": [
    {"title": "Left", "type": "object", "properties": {"a": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["a"]},
    null,
    {"title": "Right", "type": "object", "properties": {"b": {"type": "string"}}, "required": ["b"]}
  ]},
  "CancelRequestNotification": {"type": "object", "x-side": "protocol", "x-method": "$/cancel_request"}
}}
